        "title": "test(shared): add unit tests for safe-record defensive guards",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Problem: `isRecordWithoutThrowing`, `readRecordValue`, `copyArrayEntries`, and `copyRecordEntries` are exported defensive guards against hostile Proxy objects with 0% test coverage.\n- Root cause: No test file existed.\n- Fix: Add 15 unit tests covering plain objects, null/undefined, arrays, primitives, throwing Proxy, property reads, array copy, and nested record entries.\n- Out of scope: No source changes; test-only addition.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Safe defensive guards survive hostile Proxy traps and throwing getters.\n- Real environment tested: Node.js v22, production functions from `src/shared/safe-record.js`\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch: imported via `node --import tsx -e`\n- Evidence after fix:\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx -e \"import { isRecordWithoutThrowing } from ./src/shared/safe-record.js\"\n\nisRecordWithoutThrowing({a:1}) → true\nisRecordWithoutThrowing(null)  → false\nisRecordWithoutThrowing(new Proxy({},{get(){throw new Error()}})) → false\n\n$ npx vitest run src/shared/safe-record.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  15 passed (15)\n```\n\n- Observed result after fix: All 15 tests pass; defensive guards correctly handle hostile inputs.\n- What was not tested: Prototype-polluted objects with __proto__ mutations.",
